{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929928-i-don-t-understand-control-transform-create-energy","id":929928,"title":"I don't understand Control/Transform/Create Energy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T13:15:29-07:00","id":929928,"title":"I don't understand Control/Transform/Create Energy","content":"Specifically, how the spells relate to Fire, Heat, and Scale Factor.<br /> <br /> So, say a mage is in front of a bonfire, and they want to make it grow to an Inferno that envelopes the surrounding terrain using 'Control Fire'<br /> <br /> 1) Does this require increasing the scale factor?<br /> 2) What is the base 'heat' of a fire supposed to be? I thought it might be simple enough to simply slide it across the scale (IE, a level 2 Fire burns with level 2 heat) but on any kind of close inspection this is obviously ridiculous (a torch is a <b>lot</b> hotter than body temperature - hell, a lighter is for that matter.)<br /> 3) What does this line in 'Create Energy' mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For fire, assume the heat is +1 for Potency 1\u20132, +2 for Potency 3\u20134 and +3 for Potency 5+ </div> </div> </div>I feel like that might have the answer to my question if I'm parsing it correctly (Level 1 or 2 fires have heat of 2 or 3, Level 3/4 have 5/6, and level 5 has 8)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:30:51-07:00","id":929938,"title":"","content":"Fires in nWoD have two traits, Heat and Size. These are detailed on page 224 of Mage 2e (and there's a bookmark for fire.) They do base damage for Size, increased by a modifier for Heat.<br /> <br /> <i>Fire</i> Heat is not the same as <i>Heat heat</i>, so it may be better to refer to Fire Heat as <i>Intensity</i> or something like that.<br /> <br /> The entries on the Transform Energy chart (roughly) correspond with Sizes; the note on Create Energy seems to indicate that a created fire's &quot;intensity&quot; modifier scales with Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T15:15:07-07:00","id":929994,"title":"","content":"<b>Control Fire: </b>Targets an existing fire (which must be able to be affected by the spell's Scale factor) and move it a number of steps up either of these two charts equal to Potency:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Size of Fire</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Damage</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Torch</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Bonfire</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Inferno</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Heat of Fire</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Damage Modifier</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Candle (first-degree burns)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">\u2013</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Torch (second-degree burns)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Bunsen burner (third-degree burns)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Checmical fire/molten metal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">+3</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Transform Energy:</b> Targets energy from an existing source (which must be able to be affected by the spell's Scale factor) from any column on the following chart, in a row with level equal to Potency and changes it into energy from any other column in the same row, or one row up or down the chart per Reach. For an additional Reach, change the source of energy into two sources of energy with total level equal to [Potency + or - Reach).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Level</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Light</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Sound</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Heat (Celsius)</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Electricity</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Fire</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Flashlight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Casual talk</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Room temp. (22)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Car battery</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Lighter</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Ambient sunlight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Scream</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Body temp. (37)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Wall socket</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Torch</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Car headlight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Electric guitar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Kills bacteria (71)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Electric fence</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Bonfire</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Floodlight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Gunshot</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Boiling (100)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Junction box</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Inferno</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Stadium lights</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Industrial</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Books burn (233)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Main line</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Forest fire</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Create Energy: </b>Targets an area (which must be able to be affected by the spell's Scale factor) and creates energy from any column of the above chart, from a row equal to Potency, within the area. If you create fire, its damage modifier (as per the Heat of Fire Chart) is equal to [Reach/2], rounded up, to a maximum of +3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-11-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T22:31:55-07:00","id":930179,"title":"","content":"Thank you both very much. I had entirely missed the separate section for Fire intensity and was trying to figure it out based on the Transform Energy chart alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:34:30-07:00","id":988600,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necroing, but question: does a lighter flame count as a torch? Or smaller (as is, Size 0; damage 0).<br /> Because if you look at the Size chart, it always does one less damage than the level on Transform Energy.<br /> Also, Charlaquin-sama, it's [Potency/2] for the damage modifier. Thought I'd point the typo...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:37:05-07:00","id":988603,"title":"","content":"It'd be less than a torch since it's such a small flame and torches (At least what I see in movies) are usually about the size of your fist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:09:18-07:00","id":988642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929928-i-don-t-understand-control-transform-create-energy?p=988603#post988603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be less than a torch since it's such a small flame and torches (At least what I see in movies) are usually about the size of your fist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So damage 0 unless Control Fire is also used?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T21:44:26-07:00","id":988691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HTaiji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/929928-i-don-t-understand-control-transform-create-energy?p=988642#post988642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So damage 0 unless Control Fire is also used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. While a lighter can be used to start larger, more dangerous fires, it isn't that dangerous in and of itself. You can burn yourself with a lighter, sure, but the damage is going to be pretty superficial unless it maintains contact for a bit or the fire spreads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}